Not without significant fiddling with Mersenne Twister's guts. The 
problem is that Duplicate NetHack doesn't just need a repeatable series 
of random numbers, it needs a repeatable series of random numbers *for 
every different circumstance in which a random number is used*. Which 
means that if the RNG involves a complex internal state, several 
thousand copies of that state will appear in saved games. Mersenne 
Twister has a footprint of 4kb, which is too much.

